@startuml
title Stage 0.5 - Pipeline Components and Ownership

package "Stage 0.5" {
  [SyntheticInputSource or RTSP Stub] as InputSource
  [DecodeNode\n(Thread 1)] as DecodeNode
  [DummyDetectionNode\n(Thread 2)] as DetectionNode
  [OutputNode\n(Thread 3)] as OutputNode

  [FrameMetadataStoreInterface] as FrameMetadataStore
  [FrameBufferStoreInterface] as FrameBufferStore
  [ObjectMetadataStoreInterface] as ObjectMetadataStore
  [ChannelRuntimeMetaStoreInterface] as ChannelRuntimeMetaStore
  [NodeRuntimeStateStoreInterface] as NodeRuntimeStateStore
  [BoundedPointerQueue<FrameMetadata*>] as FrameQueue
  [SimpleLogger] as Logger
}

DecodeNode --> InputSource : acquire frame data
DecodeNode --> FrameMetadataStore : acquire / release FrameMetadata*
DecodeNode --> FrameBufferStore : acquire / view / release FrameBufferHandle
DecodeNode --> FrameQueue : push(FrameMetadata*)
DecodeNode --> NodeRuntimeStateStore : increment in/out/drop counters
DecodeNode --> Logger : start/stop + drop/write events

DetectionNode --> FrameQueue : pop()
DetectionNode --> ObjectMetadataStore : acquire/release ObjectMetadataHandle
DetectionNode --> FrameMetadataStore : add object handle references
DetectionNode --> ChannelRuntimeMetaStore : Write(last_seen_*, decode policy)
DetectionNode --> NodeRuntimeStateStore : increment in/out/drop counters
DetectionNode --> Logger : sample detections + drops

OutputNode --> FrameQueue : pop()
OutputNode --> ChannelRuntimeMetaStore : Read(presence TTL)
OutputNode --> FrameBufferStore : release(handle)
OutputNode --> ObjectMetadataStore : release(object handles)
OutputNode --> FrameMetadataStore : release(FrameMetadata*)
OutputNode --> NodeRuntimeStateStore : increment in/out/drop counters
OutputNode --> Logger : summary + drop logging

note bottom of FrameQueue
Overflow policy: DropOldestItem (pointer only)
Dropped pointer must be released via stores
end note

note right of ChannelRuntimeMetaStore
Store owns ChannelRuntimeMeta structures
Mutex-backed access controls read/write closures
TTL helpers enable presence checks
end note

note right of NodeRuntimeStateStore
Store owns node-level counters (in/out/drop/error)
Nodes do not store counters internally
end note

@enduml
